course: dictionary
lesson: 15459
title: A stimulus makes something react
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stimulus is something that makes a living thing react or act. Light, sound, heat and touch are all stimuli. The thing that happens because of the stimulus is the response. «Touching the hot pan made Sam pull his hand away.» The hot pan is the stimulus, and pulling the hand away is the response.
explain: Stimulus is a noun, and its plural is stimuli, so two or more of them are stimuli. «The loud bang and the bright flash were two strong stimuli.» To check your meaning, swap in "something that causes a reaction". If the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
explain: The word has other meanings too. Something that encourages activity or growth, such as a reward, can be a stimulus. In money news, a stimulus is money a government spends to help the economy grow. Read the words around the word to decide which meaning fits.
fact: A stimulus is something that causes a living thing to react.
fact: Light, sound, heat, touch and taste can all be stimuli.
fact: The plural of «stimulus» is «stimuli».
fact: Plant shoots grow towards light, so light is a stimulus for them.
fact: In money news, a «stimulus» is government money spent to help the economy grow.
exercise: In «The bright light made the cat blink», what is the stimulus? | The cat blinking | The cat's tail | *The bright light | The sleepy room
exercise: What is the plural of «stimulus»? | stimulators | *stimuli | stimulies | stimulus
exercise: When you touch a hot pan and pull your hand away, what is the response? | The hot pan | The stimulus | *Pulling your hand away | Feeling warm
test: «Plants grow towards light, so light is a stimulus for them.» What does stimulus mean in this sentence? | *Something that causes a living thing to react | A kind of food | A type of plant | A loud noise only
test: Which of these is a stimulus for your ears? | A closed door | *A sudden loud bang | A soft pillow | A sleepy cat
exam: In «The government gave a stimulus to help shops reopen», what does stimulus mean? | A loud noise | *Money spent to help the economy grow | A kind of light | Something that makes you sneeze
